{"type":"message","id":"b278573e","parentId":"244a2b8f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:28:40.342Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So SSH is not running at all. The user is asking why SSH is not available after upgrading to OpenClaw 5.19. Let me check the healthcheck skill and also look at what OpenClaw 5.19 might have changed, and check if there's a way to restart SSH or if OpenClaw manages SSH.\n\nWait - this is running inside a container (Linux 95158cabb9c3). This appears to be the OpenClaw node itself. Let me check if OpenClaw manages SSH access.\n\nLet me check the healthcheck skill and also look at the gateway status to understand the setup.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-39a34545-2bb7-4770-a1fc-a538708ecba3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"path\":\"/app/skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c41a4599-a125-4c8a-b543-6f7a4ac6efb4","name":"exec","arguments":{"timeout":10,"command":"openclaw gateway status 2>&1 | head -40"},"partialArgs":"{\"timeout\":10,\"command\":\"openclaw gateway status 2>&1 | head -40\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":13208,"output":202,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13506,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779337715713,"responseId":"chatcmpl-33514c02-8aab-4dce-86af-8f55131410aa"}}
{"type":"message","id":"957db846","parentId":"b278573e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:28:45.043Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-39a34545-2bb7-4770-a1fc-a538708ecba3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: healthcheck\ndescription: \"Audit/harden OpenClaw hosts: SSH, firewall, updates, exposure, backups, disk encryption, gateway security.\"\n---\n\n# OpenClaw host healthcheck\n\nGoal: assess host risk, run read-only checks, then propose staged hardening without breaking access.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Ask before state-changing actions.\n- Do not change SSH/firewall/remote access until access path is confirmed.\n- Prefer reversible steps and rollback notes.\n- Never claim OpenClaw manages OS firewall, SSH, or updates.\n- If identity/role unknown, recommend only.\n- User choices: numbered list.\n- Never print secrets.\n\n## Context to infer first\n\n- OS/version, container vs host.\n- Privilege level.\n- Access path: local, SSH, RDP, tailnet.\n- Network exposure: public IP, reverse proxy, tunnel, LAN only.\n- OpenClaw gateway status, bind, auth.\n- Backup status.\n- Disk encryption.\n- Automatic security updates.\n- Usage mode: personal workstation, local assistant box, remote server, other.\n\nAsk only for missing facts. Simple phrasing preferred.\n\n## Read-only checks\n\nAsk once for permission to run read-only checks. Then run relevant commands.\n\nCommon:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw security audit --deep\nopenclaw gateway status --deep\nopenclaw doctor\n```\n\nmacOS:\n\n```bash\nsw_vers\nlsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN\n/usr/libexec/ApplicationFirewall/socketfilterfw --getglobalstate\npfctl -s info\ntmutil status\nfdesetup status\nsoftwareupdate --schedule\n```\n\nLinux:\n\n```bash\ncat /etc/os-release\nss -ltnup || ss -ltnp\nufw status || firewall-cmd --state || nft list ruleset\nsystemctl status ssh sshd\nlsblk -f\n```\n\nWindows:\n\n```powershell\nsysteminfo\nGet-NetFirewallProfile\nGet-BitLockerVolume\n```\n\n## Risk profile\n\nAfter context is known, ask desired posture:\n\n1. Convenience: local/private, minimal prompts.\n2. Balanced: secure defaults, low friction.\n3. Strict: remote/public/sensitive data, more lock-down.\n\n## Report shape\n\n- Current posture: one paragraph.\n- Findings: severity + evidence + why it matters.\n- Recommended plan: staged, reversible.\n- Commands: read-only first; write actions only after approval.\n- Gaps: what could not be checked.\n\n## Hardening menu\n\nOffer only relevant items:\n\n- Bind gateway to loopback/LAN/tailnet intentionally.\n- Require auth for remote access.\n- Close public ports or restrict by firewall.\n- Enable OS security updates.\n- Enable disk encryption.\n- Verify backups and restore path.\n- Disable password SSH or require keys/MFA where appropriate.\n- Add scheduled `openclaw security audit --deep`.\n\nConfirm exact action before applying.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779337725041}}
{"type":"message","id":"6d5d53ef","parentId":"957db846","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:28:45.045Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-c41a4599-a125-4c8a-b543-6f7a4ac6efb4","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Service: systemd user (disabled)\nFile logs: /tmp/openclaw/openclaw-2026-05-21.log\n\nConfig (cli): ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\nConfig (service): ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n\nGateway: bind=loopback (127.0.0.1), port=18789 (env/config)\nProbe target: ws://127.0.0.1:18789\nDashboard: http://127.0.0.1:18789/\nProbe note: Loopback-only gateway; only local clients can connect.\n\nCLI version: 2026.5.19 (/usr/local/bin/openclaw)\nGateway version: 2026.5.19\n\nRuntime: unknown (systemctl not available; systemd user services are required on Linux.)\nConnectivity probe: ok\nCapability: admin-capable\n\nsystemd user services unavailable.\nsystemd user services are unavailable; install/enable systemd or run the gateway under your supervisor.\nIf you're in a container, run the gateway in the foreground instead of `openclaw gateway`.\n\nListening: *:18789\nTroubles: run openclaw status\nTroubleshooting: https://docs.openclaw.ai/troubleshooting"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":4684,"aggregated":"Service: systemd user (disabled)\nFile logs: /tmp/openclaw/openclaw-2026-05-21.log\n\nConfig (cli): ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\nConfig (service): ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n\nGateway: bind=loopback (127.0.0.1), port=18789 (env/config)\nProbe target: ws://127.0.0.1:18789\nDashboard: http://127.0.0.1:18789/\nProbe note: Loopback-only gateway; only local clients can connect.\n\nCLI version: 2026.5.19 (/usr/local/bin/openclaw)\nGateway version: 2026.5.19\n\nRuntime: unknown (systemctl not available; systemd user services are required on Linux.)\nConnectivity probe: ok\nCapability: admin-capable\n\nsystemd user services unavailable.\nsystemd user services are unavailable; install/enable systemd or run the gateway under your supervisor.\n