{"type":"message","id":"30be11d4","parentId":"c83968e9","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:29:12.638Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see now. The user is asking about SSH not working after upgrading to OpenClaw 5.19. But looking at this environment, SSH doesn't seem to be running at all. This is a container environment (Debian 12 inside a Linux 5.4 kernel). There's no SSH daemon running.\n\nThe user's question might be about:\n1. The host system's SSH (not this container)\n2. Or maybe they're confused about what OpenClaw 5.19 changed\n\nLet me think about what OpenClaw 5.19 might have changed related to SSH. OpenClaw typically manages its own gateway on port 18789, but SSH is a system service. They're separate things.\n\n\nActually, I should clarify the architecture here—the gateway running on port 18789 is OpenClaw's own service, not SSH. Since I'm in a container without SSH running at all, the user might be referring to their host system or misidentifying which service is affected by the upgrade.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n我需要先了解更多信息来定位问题。请先运行以下命令，把结果发给我：\n\n**在出问题的机器上运行：**\n```bash\nopenclaw gateway status\nsshd -v 2>&1 | head -5\nsystemctl status ssh 2>&1 || service ssh status 2>&1\njournalctl -u ssh --no-pager -n 20 2>&1\n```\n\n同时，帮你查一下 OpenClaw 5.19 的变更日志：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-1d99dba1-076f-48c5-8a22-606775aab1aa","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"OpenClaw 5.19 changelog ssh changes"},"partialArgs":"{\"query\":\"OpenClaw 5.19 changelog ssh changes\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":13320,"output":337,"cacheRead":912,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14569,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779337739231,"responseId":"chatcmpl-4fb41c10-d919-4e52-b2f9-e0f653e43a51"}}
